<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The shoulder pads' ability, granted by their CompAbilitiesApparel. The rules are in
    HemophageWarcasket.Ability_Dismember, the walk, warmup, strike and drain in
    JobDriver_Dismember (JobDefs/Dismember.xml), the strike's damage in
    DamageDefs/Dismember.xml and its combat log line in RulePackDefs/Combat_Dismember.xml.

    The strike takes hold of one whole arm or leg the target still has, at random, whatever
    its armor, and tears it off unless the limb is too sturdy. A target that has lost them all
    has its head taken instead. Any pawn with a limb can be targeted, downed or not,
    mechanoids and animals included, and hostile or not while canTargetNonHostile is true.
    What counts as a limb is DismemberTarget's rule (its header): a centipede's two last body
    rings do, taken from the tail in.

    damage 60 is what the strike does to that one part, times the pilot's MeleeDamageFactor
    and the target's IncomingDamageFactor (Ability_Dismember.Strike.cs has the sum). A limb with
    more health left than that is wounded and stays on. 60 is twice a human limb's 30, so a
    Tough target, who takes half damage, still loses it, and only one who stacks the robust
    gene on that (22.5) keeps the limb. It is about two blows of a zeushammer (31), from a
    strike that takes a second to wind up and a component to reload. A limb's health is its
    part's hitPoints times the race's health scale, so of the big bodies a megaspider's leg
    (50) and a muffalo's (53) come off, a centipede's last ring (87) only for a pilot in the
    hemogen rush, whose melee damage factor of 1.5 makes the strike 90, and a thrumbo's leg
    (240) takes three strikes even then. The head goes by the same damage: a human's (25)
    comes off, a centipede's (130) takes three strikes or two in the rush.
    aimHeightComp and aimHeightField are unset here: they name where another mod keeps a
    melee aim height for the strike to follow, and that mod's compat root adds them
    (1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/Dismember.xml).

    Targeting: range is unset and requireLineOfSight off because the click is not range
    limited; the pilot walks to the target and the job enforces reach and sight at
    distanceToTarget 1.9, touching with diagonals. Who is a valid target is decided in
    ValidateTarget, not here.

    castTime 60 (1 s) is the windup, half of Bloodfeed's, since this is used mid-fight; the
    target is held for it, as vanilla's touch abilities hold theirs.

    The limit is the pads' strikes, not a timer: each cast spends one of the two the pads'
    CompApparelReloadable holds (WarcasketShoulders_Hemophage.xml has the pool and its
    price), so cooldownTime 0 lets one strike follow another, as the family's stocked
    abilities do. gizmoClass adds the "strikes / max" count in the button's top right corner,
    where vanilla draws a reloadable's.

    The rest of DismemberExtension is the drain, which follows the strike when the pilot is
    hemogenic and the target is humanlike and bleeding, as one whose limb came off is and one
    whose limb held mostly is, with the target held throughout. It is Bloodfeed
    spread over drainTicks 240 (4 s): hemogenGain 0.2 is Bloodfeed's 20 hemogen, scaled by
    the target's body size as a bite is, and targetBloodLoss 0.4499 is the blood loss a bite
    causes, on top of the stump's own bleeding. A drain cut short keeps what it collected.
    A target that dies, to the strike or during the drain, is drained on as a corpse for the
    blood it has left, and one that died of blood loss has none (Ability_Dismember.Drain.cs).
    A bloodfeeder is not drained, as Bloodfeed refuses one. drainSources, feedingHediffs and
    hemohunterStates are unset here: they widen the drain for another mod's feeding genes
    and hand its hunting mental state the strike, so each is added by that mod's compat root
    (1.6/Mods/VanillaRacesExpandedSanguophage/Patches/DismemberFeeding.xml). hemohunterStrikes
    true is the switch on the last, on by default because a pilot who goes hunting in this
    suit is meant to be the worse for it, and off for a player who wants the plain bite back.
    hemohunterHuntsByGene true widens that hunt from the bite's prey to whatever the pilot's
    drainSources open to it, a corpse found lying among them: the feeding genes say what a
    pilot can feed on, and a hunter in that state holds to no diet. Off, the hunt keeps to
    the bite's prey.
    bloodFilthCount 10 within bloodFilthRadius 2 is the spatter a strike throws when its
    part comes off: the 13 cells of a radius 2 disc, so about seven of them catch some, a
    repeat on a cell thickening it. The filth is the target's own blood, so a mechanoid
    throws machine bits and a bloodless race nothing.
    decapitateBodiesWithoutLimbs false leaves a body built with no limbs at all (a termite, a
    diabolus, a war queen, a devourer) an invalid target: beheading it would kill it outright
    on first use. decapitateWithoutLimbsMaxBodySize 0.5 exempts the small ones, which lose
    their head whatever the switch says: a cobra (body size 0.25) dies to any one hit, so
    there is nothing to protect. Limbless bodies fall on either side of a wide gap, the
    smallest of the large ones being the termite at 1.6, and half a human's size sits in it.

    The mod settings override castTime, cooldownTime, the pads' pool and the
    DismemberExtension fields that Settings_Dismember.cs and Settings_Sanguophage.cs under
    Source/1.6/Settings/ list, damage and hemohunterStrikes among them.

    showUndrafted as on the hemogen rush. No castSound: the damage plays its own impact, and
    the drain plays Bloodfeed's.
  -->
  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
    <defName>HPWC_Dismember</defName>
    <label>dismember</label>
    <description>Tear an arm or a leg off a nearby target, whatever armor it wears. A limb too sturdy to tear off will only be wounded, and a target with no limbs left will lose its head instead. If the pilot is hemogenic and the target is human, the pilot will then hold on and drain hemogen from the wound, which will also cause the target to lose blood.</description>
    <abilityClass>HemophageWarcasket.Ability_Dismember</abilityClass>
    <gizmoClass>HemophageWarcasket.Command_Dismember</gizmoClass>
    <iconPath>UI/Abilities/WarcasketHemophage/Dismember</iconPath>
    <jobDef>HPWC_Dismember</jobDef>
    <jobReportString>Tearing off a limb.</jobReportString>
    <targetMode>Pawn</targetMode>
    <targetingParametersList>
      <li>
        <canTargetPawns>true</canTargetPawns>
        <canTargetHumans>true</canTargetHumans>
        <canTargetAnimals>true</canTargetAnimals>
        <canTargetMechs>true</canTargetMechs>
        <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
        <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
        <canTargetLocations>false</canTargetLocations>
      </li>
    </targetingParametersList>
    <distanceToTarget>1.9</distanceToTarget>
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <castTime>60</castTime>
    <cooldownTime>0</cooldownTime>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="HemophageWarcasket.DismemberExtension">
        <damage>60</damage>
        <drainTicks>240</drainTicks>
        <hemogenGain>0.2</hemogenGain>
        <targetBloodLoss>0.4499</targetBloodLoss>
        <bloodFilthCount>10</bloodFilthCount>
        <bloodFilthRadius>2</bloodFilthRadius>
        <canTargetNonHostile>true</canTargetNonHostile>
        <decapitateBodiesWithoutLimbs>false</decapitateBodiesWithoutLimbs>
        <decapitateWithoutLimbsMaxBodySize>0.5</decapitateWithoutLimbsMaxBodySize>
        <hemohunterStrikes>true</hemohunterStrikes>
        <hemohunterHuntsByGene>true</hemohunterHuntsByGene>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
</Defs>
